# Dynamic branch sizing

Try adding another sentence to the longer branch. Its box grows and moves outward; neighbouring branches adjust to leave room. Remove the sentence and the layout becomes compact again.

@animate
# Explaining a system
- Requests
  - A client sends a request
- Authentication
  - Verify the supplied credentials before allowing access to protected resources
  - Return a clear error when credentials are missing or invalid
- Caching and keeping stored responses up to date
  - A cached response can avoid repeating an expensive database query when the requested data has not changed
  - When the source data changes, invalidate the affected cache entry so the next request rebuilds it from current data
  - Give temporary cache entries an expiry time
- Storage
  - Store the durable data
- Background jobs
  - Put slow work in a queue
- Response
  - Send the result to the client
@end
